# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# POLYBOT — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the section matching your
# account type. NEVER commit the actual .env file to GitHub.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Step 1: Set your signature type ──────────────────────────
# This is the ONE thing that determines which fields below you
# actually need. Pick based on how you use Polymarket:
#
#   0 = EOA           — You trade with a raw wallet private key
#                        directly (MetaMask/hardware wallet used
#                        as-is, no Polymarket account layer).
#                        Uncommon for normal Polymarket users.
#
#   1 = POLY_PROXY     — You log into Polymarket with EMAIL or
#                        Magic Link. Most common for everyday
#                        Polymarket users who signed up with email.
#
#   2 = POLY_GNOSIS_SAFE — You log into Polymarket by CONNECTING A
#                        BROWSER WALLET (MetaMask, Coinbase Wallet,
#                        Rabby) through the Polymarket website's
#                        "Connect Wallet" button.
#
#   3 = POLY_1271      — The newer "deposit wallet" flow Polymarket
#                        now recommends for brand-new API users
#                        (accounts created after ~April 2026).
#                        ⚠ NOT RECOMMENDED RIGHT NOW: as of June
#                        2026 there is a confirmed, still-open SDK
#                        bug where every order gets rejected with
#                        "the order signer address has to be the
#                        address of the API KEY" regardless of
#                        correct setup (py-clob-client-v2 issues
#                        #70 and #75). If your account uses this
#                        flow, use signature_type=2 instead as a
#                        working alternative until Polymarket fixes
#                        the SDK — see README Pre-Flight Checklist.
#
# If you're not sure which you are: if you signed up with email,
# use 1. If you connected a browser wallet, use 2.
WALLET_SIGNATURE_TYPE=1

# ── Step 2: Fill in ONLY the section matching your type above ─
# The bot only reads the fields relevant to WALLET_SIGNATURE_TYPE.
# You can leave the other sections' values as placeholders —
# they're ignored — but PRIVATE_KEY is always required.

# ── Required for ALL signature types ───────────────────────────
# Your wallet's private key — this is the key that SIGNS orders.
# For type 0: this is your trading wallet's own key.
# For types 1/2/3: this is the key behind your Polymarket login
#   (the Magic-exported key for email accounts, or your browser
#   wallet's key) — NOT a separate "bot wallet."
PRIVATE_KEY=your_wallet_private_key_here

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ABOUT API CREDENTIALS — there is no field for these below,
# and that's intentional. You never manually generate an API
# key. The bot derives it programmatically from PRIVATE_KEY on
# every startup (deterministic — same key every time, safe to
# re-run). Check preflight.py's output or
# data/derived_api_creds.json (created automatically) if you
# ever need to see the derived key, e.g. for a support ticket.
#
# ⚠ IF YOU ARE TYPE 1 (POLY_PROXY / email-Magic account):
# DO NOT generate an API key through polymarket.com/settings.
# Confirmed upstream bug — website-generated keys for these
# accounts get registered under your PROXY wallet address, but
# CLOB V2 validates by your SIGNER (EOA) address, so the two
# can never match and every order returns 401 regardless of
# correct setup. Always let this bot derive credentials itself
# (the default, automatic behavior) rather than pasting in a
# website-generated key.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Type 0 (EOA) — funder not used for TRADING, but see note ──
# Not needed for order placement: orders settle directly against
# your EOA, and you can leave FUNDER_ADDRESS blank for that purpose.
# However, position RECONCILIATION (the bot double-checking its own
# bookkeeping against what you actually hold on-chain) queries by
# wallet address — if you want that feature to work for an EOA
# account, set FUNDER_ADDRESS to your EOA's own public address here.
# Trading itself still works fine either way.
# You DO need to set on-chain pUSD + conditional token allowances
# once before trading — see README Pre-Flight Checklist.

# ── Type 1 (POLY_PROXY) — email/Magic accounts ─────────────────
# FUNDER = the Polymarket proxy wallet address that actually holds
# your funds (visible in your Polymarket account/profile page —
# NOT your email or the raw Magic-exported EOA address).
FUNDER_ADDRESS=your_polymarket_proxy_wallet_address_here

# ── Type 2 (POLY_GNOSIS_SAFE) — browser wallet accounts ────────
# FUNDER = the same field as above (FUNDER_ADDRESS) — this is your
# Polymarket Safe-proxy wallet address, shown on your profile page
# when you're connected via a browser wallet. Different from your
# MetaMask/browser wallet's own address.
# (Uses the same FUNDER_ADDRESS variable as type 1 above.)

# ── Type 3 (POLY_1271) — deposit wallet accounts ───────────────
# FUNDER = your deposit wallet address (shown on your Polymarket
# profile page for accounts using this newer flow).
# (Also uses FUNDER_ADDRESS above — not recommended right now,
# see the warning under WALLET_SIGNATURE_TYPE.)

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Quick reference — what FUNDER_ADDRESS means per type:
#   Type 0: not used (leave FUNDER_ADDRESS as placeholder)
#   Type 1: your Polymarket proxy wallet address
#   Type 2: your Polymarket Safe-proxy wallet address
#   Type 3: your Polymarket deposit wallet address
# All three (1/2/3) addresses are found on your Polymarket
# profile/account page, NOT in your browser wallet extension.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
